## Summary

I idiomized `rs/fq/src/performance_log.rs` along three axes. **Naming**: the column-index enum is now `PerflogColumn` (no `_enum` suffix, no module-prefix on each variant), with PascalCase variants — `perflog_is_client` → `IsClient`, `perflog_nb_packets_received` → `NbPacketsReceived`, etc. Constants (`PER_LOG_VERSION`, `PERF_LOG_MAX_ITEMS`) were already SCREAMING_SNAKE and stay as-is. **API shape**: the two free functions whose primary argument was a "self" became methods — `perflog_param_name(rank)` collapsed into `PerflogColumn::param_name(self)`, and `perflog_setup(quic, name)` became `quic_t::perflog_setup(&mut self, name)` (the call mutates `quic.perflog_fn` / `v_perflog_ctx`, so this is the natural method receiver). **Documentation**: doc comments were rewritten to lead with what the Rust API does, with `C: picoquic_*` cites at the end for traceability rather than as the only description; the constant docs gained explicit `C:` cites too. `quic_t` itself was left alone — it's owned by `internal.rs` and renaming it is a project-wide change out of scope for this per-header pass, matching the precedent set by `cc_common.rs`. No callers in sibling modules referenced any of the renamed items, so the change is self-contained.


